          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.55,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "and I'll not add anything to the dom here for now at least.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 16.47,
          "en": "Now my goal is to instead create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.47,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "that alert component dynamically and show it dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.93,
          "en": "and dynamically, it's the wrong word maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.93,
          "end": 24.993,
          "en": "I mean programmatically from inside code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "Now, for that, we first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 30.333,
          "en": "need a new method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 32.97,
          "en": "because now we have to write some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 34.71,
          "en": "to show the error alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 37.727,
          "en": "And I'll turn this into a private method, showErrorAlert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "I added this to the off component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 47.01,
          "en": "and show error alert has to be called whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.01,
          "end": 47.91,
          "en": "we have an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.91,
          "end": 50.55,
          "en": "So here, when we set the error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.55,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "we now have to call this show error alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 56.37,
          "en": "And of course we could now also change to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.37,
          "end": 59.82,
          "en": "get general flow, to not set the error globally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.82,
          "end": 63.18,
          "en": "on a property here, but instead pass it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.18,
          "end": 66.27,
          "en": "into show error alert. And that is what I will do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.27,
          "end": 69.57,
          "en": "I'll still set it globally because we used that in the past,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.57,
          "end": 71.19,
          "en": "but you wouldn't need that now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.19,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "because this error property now has no real use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 77.78999999999999,
          "en": "because we're not using it in the template anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 80.25,
          "en": "Still, I'll leave it here because we used it in the past",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.25,
          "end": 83.16,
          "en": "but you don't need it anymore for this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.16,
          "end": 87.21000000000001,
          "en": "Instead show error alert will receive the message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.21000000000001,
          "end": 88.37,
          "en": "So let's accept it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.37,
          "end": 90.21000000000001,
          "en": "It will be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.21000000000001,
          "end": 93.45,
          "en": "And in here the goal now is to dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.45,
          "end": 96.60300000000001,
          "en": "create our alert component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "Now for this you manually need to instantiate a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 104.64,
          "en": "Now, a simple approach you could take,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.64,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "would be that you import your alert component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 111.3,
          "en": "So you go to the shared folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.3,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "import it from the alert folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 117.39,
          "en": "and then from there you import the alert component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 119.22,
          "en": "Now we have access to the alert component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.22,
          "end": 121.23,
          "en": "which we defined in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.23,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "And now of course, you could think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "that you simply create alert component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 128.04,
          "en": "and save it an alert CMP constant maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 129.96,
          "en": "by calling new alert component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.96,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "It is a class after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134.16,
          "en": "Now this is valid TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.16,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "but it is not valid Angular code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "This will not throw an error if you compile it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 141.93,
          "en": "but it also won't work in any way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 144.09,
          "en": "You can't work with that alert component then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.09,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "in the way Angular needs to work with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.94,
          "end": 148.92000000000002,
          "en": "because Angular does a lot more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.92000000000002,
          "end": 152.91,
          "en": "than just create an object when it instantiates a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.91,
          "end": 154.26,
          "en": "It needs to wire it up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.26,
          "end": 157.65,
          "en": "It needs to wire it up to change detection into the dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.65,
          "end": 160.35,
          "en": "This year, would be a normal JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.35,
          "end": 162.75,
          "en": "and that is not what Angular needs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.75,
          "end": 166.77,
          "en": "So therefore, you can't create your own component like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.77,
          "end": 169.383,
          "en": "This year won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 174.09,
          "en": "Instead, you need to let Angular create this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.09,
          "end": 176.57999999999998,
          "en": "And for that, Angular gives you a tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.57999999999998,
          "end": 179.22,
          "en": "the component factory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "To get access to that tool, you need to inject something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 185.13,
          "en": "and you don't inject the component factory itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.13,
          "end": 190.13,
          "en": "Instead, you inject a component factory resolver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 193.14,
          "en": "Now of course it is up to you how you name that argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.14,
          "end": 195.42,
          "en": "And again, I'm using that trick here where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.42,
          "end": 198.18,
          "en": "this automatically gets stored in a private property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.18,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "It's up to you how you name this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 204.12,
          "en": "but the type thereafter is component factory resolver",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 205.14,
          "en": "and that's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.14,
          "end": 209.04,
          "en": "It has to be the resolver, not the component factory itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.04,
          "end": 211.44,
          "en": "Component factory resolver is then imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 212.703,
          "en": "from at Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 217.62,
          "en": "Now with the component factory resolver injected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.62,
          "end": 221.49,
          "en": "in show error alert, you now use that resolver to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 221.49,
          "end": 223.5,
          "en": "get access to component factory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 223.5,
          "end": 224.7,
          "en": "Yeah, sounds strange, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 226.92000000000002,
          "en": "But this is how the flow works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 226.92000000000002,
          "end": 230.34,
          "en": "So there, you now use the component factory resolver",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.34,
          "end": 233.28,
          "en": "and there you have a resolved component factory method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 233.28,
          "end": 235.86,
          "en": "which gives you access to a component factory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 235.86,
          "end": 237.66,
          "en": "as provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 237.66,
          "end": 239.94,
          "en": "Now to that factory you have to pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 239.94,
          "end": 241.74,
          "en": "the type of your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 241.74,
          "end": 244.86,
          "en": "which in our case here would be the alert component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 244.86,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "Now you don't instantiate this, you don't have new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 249.6,
          "en": "in front of this or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 249.6,
          "end": 251.34,
          "en": "You just pass on the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 251.34,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "So the angler knows where to look for that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 256.353,
          "en": "which it then should create for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 257.61,
          "end": 262.263,
          "en": "This method here will return a component factory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 264.18,
          "end": 266.97,
          "en": "Or to be precise, and alert component factory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 266.97,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "Not the component itself, just the factory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 272.85,
          "en": "So this now is essentially an object that knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 272.85,
          "end": 274.83,
          "en": "how to create alert components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 274.83,
          "end": 276.843,
          "en": "which is a great first step at least.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 281.28,
          "en": "Now with that factory we can use that factory to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 281.28,
          "end": 283.56,
          "en": "create a concrete component, but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 283.56,
          "end": 286.92,
          "en": "for this we also need a place where we can attach it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 286.92,
          "end": 289.83,
          "en": "in our dom and we don't have that place yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 289.83,
          "end": 293.22,
          "en": "We need to tell Angler where we want to add that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 293.22,
          "end": 296.43,
          "en": "And now you could think that, you use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 296.43,
          "end": 298.71,
          "en": "some way of getting access to some element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 298.71,
          "end": 300.72,
          "en": "Let's say here we want to add it so we add a diff",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 300.72,
          "end": 304.59,
          "en": "with a local reference addHere and with at view child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 304.59,
          "end": 305.73,
          "en": "we could get access to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 305.73,
          "end": 307.92,
          "en": "as you learned earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 307.92,
          "end": 310.08,
          "en": "But this is not how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 310.08,
          "end": 313.23,
          "en": "Angular needs a view container ref, which you might remember",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 313.23,
          "end": 315.63,
          "en": "from the directive's deep dive section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 315.63,
          "end": 318.78,
          "en": "A view container ref is essentially an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 318.78,
          "end": 321.15,
          "en": "managed internally by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 321.15,
          "end": 325.02,
          "en": "which gives Angular a reference, a pointer to a place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 325.02,
          "end": 327.78,
          "en": "in the dom you could say, with which it can interact.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 327.78,
          "end": 329.55,
          "en": "And this object has more than just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 329.55,
          "end": 331.74,
          "en": "like the coordinates where it sits,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 331.74,
          "end": 335.31,
          "en": "it has methods like hey please create a component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 335.31,
          "end": 337.77,
          "en": "And we need something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 337.77,
          "end": 341.64,
          "en": "Now to get access to such a view container reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 341.64,
          "end": 345.75,
          "en": "there is a nice trick or actually not, not a hack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 345.75,
          "end": 348.3,
          "en": "it's the official approach for getting access to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 348.3,
          "end": 350.523,
          "en": "we can create a helper directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 351.39,
          "end": 355.74,
          "en": "Now that directive could be named placeholder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 355.74,
          "end": 357.78,
          "en": "You can name it however you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 357.78,
          "end": 360.69,
          "en": "-: And I'll name it placeholder.directive.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 360.69,
          "end": 361.98,
          "en": "that's the file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 361.98,
          "end": 363.99,
          "en": "And in there we export a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 363.99,
          "end": 366.09,
          "en": "I created business shared folder, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 366.09,
          "end": 368.56,
          "en": "I export a class, PlaceholderDirective",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 370.56,
          "end": 374.79,
          "en": "and that will receive the @directive decorator of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 374.79,
          "end": 378.63,
          "en": "Now this @directive decorator needs one thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 378.63,
          "end": 380.46,
          "en": "and that's the selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 380.46,
          "end": 385.363,
